    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN a <description>, and it is INSIDE the root
        element on purpose - a comment ABOVE <StandardValueSet> breaks `sf` deploy at
        conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent xml file".

        PHASE 2 (2026-08-14) - 'PSA' IS BEING REPLACED BY 'Under Contract (PSA)'.
        This file is at the ADDITIVE step (P2-D1): BOTH values are present and active.
        'Under Contract (PSA)' is placed immediately after 'PSA' so that removing 'PSA'
        at P2-D3 leaves the pipeline order intact (LOI -> Under Contract (PSA) ->
        About to Close). <sorted> is false, so position here is the displayed order.

        <forecastCategory>Forecast</forecastCategory> and <probability>85</probability>
        are COPIED FROM THE OUTGOING 'PSA' ENTRY VERBATIM, not chosen. They are the whole
        reason this is a value migration rather than a new stage: forecastCategory drives
        every forecast roll-up and probability drives Expected Revenue, so a deal that
        moves from 'PSA' to 'Under Contract (PSA)' must not move in any forecast. If the
        outgoing entry is ever edited before P2-D3, re-copy - do not re-derive.

        NO %2F ENCODING APPLIES TO THIS VALUE. 'Under Contract (PSA)' contains spaces and
        parentheses but no slash. The 'Dead/Pass' entry below is LITERAL here and is
        encoded 'Dead%2FPass' only inside BusinessProcess/RecordType metadata; that
        precedent invites exactly the wrong instinct. Do not encode the parentheses.

        P2-D3 (staged, NOT applied here) sets <isActive>false</isActive> on the 'PSA'
        entry. See agent-output/p2-d3-retire-psa/.
    -->
